{
  "id": "request-logs",
  "category": "practical",
  "language": "typescript",
  "title": "Summarize API request logs",
  "eyebrow": "TypeScript · Data processing",
  "summary": "An operations team receives noisy request logs containing retries and query variants. Produce a route-level reliability report after deduplication, including request counts, 5xx error rates, and the specified latency percentile. Turn noisy request records into a concise reliability report for each route.",
  "durationMinutes": 30,
  "functionName": "summarizeRequests",
  "requirements": [
    "Deduplicate by requestId, keeping the record with the latest ISO timestamp. For tied timestamps, keep the last record in the input.",
    "Strip query strings from routes, then group by the resulting route. Sort output by route.",
    "For each route return count, errorRatePercent for HTTP 5xx responses rounded to one decimal, and p95Ms.",
    "p95Ms uses the nearest-rank method: sort latencies and select index ceil(0.95 × count) - 1.",
    "Ignore records with a status outside 100–599 or a negative/nonfinite latency."
  ],
  "starterCode": "type RequestLog = { requestId: string; timestamp: string; route: string; status: number; latencyMs: number };\ntype RouteSummary = { route: string; count: number; errorRatePercent: number; p95Ms: number };\n\nexport function summarizeRequests(logs: RequestLog[]): RouteSummary[] {\n  return [];\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "Build a Map from requestId to the latest record. Replace a record when the next timestamp is greater than or equal to the saved one.",
    "Group only valid deduplicated records by route.split(\"?\")[0].",
    "Sort numeric latencies, then choose the nearest-rank index. Round error percentage with Math.round(value * 10) / 10."
  ],
